<% layout('layouts/boilerplateAbout') %>
    <title>About | John A. Otte, PsyD</title>

    <!-- ============================== PAGE HERO ============================== -->
    <header class="page-hero">
        <div class="container">
            <p class="eyebrow">Get to know Dr. Otte</p>
            <h1 class="page-title">About John</h1>
            <div class="flourish"><i class="fas fa-star"></i></div>
            <p class="page-hero-sub">More than 35 years walking with people through addiction, depression, and the
                search for meaning, here in Denver, Colorado.</p>
        </div>
    </header>

    <!-- ============================== BIO ROWS ============================== -->
    <section class="section">
        <div class="container">

            <div class="row feature-row align-items-center g-5">
                <div class="col-lg-5" data-aos="fade-right">
                    <div class="feature-photo">
                        <img src="/images/johnpic-3.jpg" alt="Dr. John A. Otte">
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-lg-7 feature-text" data-aos="fade-left">
                    <p class="feature-kicker">Roots</p>
                    <h2 class="feature-heading">Michigan, Calvin College, and Carl Jung</h2>
                    <p>Dr. Otte grew up in western Michigan, the youngest of five children, born into a family of
                        teachers and ministers. He graduated from Calvin College, a Dutch Christian Reformed college
                        known for high academic standards. After graduating, Dr. Otte was accepted into one of the first
                        doctoral clinical psychology programs (Psy.D. degree) certified by the American Psychology
                        Association (APA). His focus in graduate school was on psychoanalytic and family systems theory,
                        with a particular interest in the theories of Carl Jung.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="row feature-row align-items-center g-5">
                <div class="col-lg-5 order-lg-2" data-aos="fade-left">
                    <div class="feature-photo">
                        <img src="/images/helping-hand.jfif" alt="Lotus flower">
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-lg-7 order-lg-1 feature-text" data-aos="fade-right">
                    <p class="feature-kicker">A turn toward spirituality</p>
                    <h2 class="feature-heading">From addiction work to a deeper practice</h2>
                    <p>Many members of Dr. Otte's family suffered from the disease of addiction, so, naturally, this
                        became a focus of his therapy. He has always had a private practice specializing in the
                        treatment of depression, addiction, and Bipolar disorder. After 15 years of practice and several
                        personal and family crises, Dr. Otte began focusing on integrating spirituality in
                        psychotherapy. This was a natural transition for him, given his family history and religious
                        upbringing. He will tell you, though, that spirituality is not synonymous with religion, and
                        that bringing spirituality into his practice profoundly changed him as a therapist.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="row feature-row align-items-center g-5">
                <div class="col-lg-5" data-aos="fade-right">
                    <div class="feature-photo">
                        <img src="/images/mountains.jfif" alt="A helping hand">
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-lg-7 feature-text" data-aos="fade-left">
                    <p class="feature-kicker">Beyond private practice</p>
                    <h2 class="feature-heading">A career across many settings</h2>
                    <p>Besides his private practice, Dr. Otte has maintained part-time clinical work in various
                        settings.
                        He directed an Employee Assistance Program for Texaco in the 90's, worked at Denver County Jail
                        for several years in the early 2000s, and has worked in several area hospitals performing
                        psychological evaluations. He currently works at Good Samaritan Medical Center half time
                        conducting evaluations.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="row feature-row align-items-center g-5">
                <div class="col-lg-5 order-lg-2" data-aos="fade-left">
                    <div class="feature-photo">
                        <img src="/images/johnpic-2.jpg" alt="Dr. John A. Otte">
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-lg-7 order-lg-1 feature-text" data-aos="fade-right">
                    <p class="feature-kicker">How he works</p>
                    <h2 class="feature-heading">Warm, irreverent, and still in love with the work</h2>
                    <p>Dr. Otte brings a warm, irreverent, and compassionate approach to therapy. He will tell you that,
                        even after 35 years, he still loves therapy and continues to learn from the people he works
                        with. For the majority of his clinical career he has offered group psychotherapy alongside
                        traditional individual work, and he continues to provide psychodynamic group therapy for those
                        brave enough to embrace the challenging and powerful modality. Most of all, Dr. Otte is awed by
                        the power of the human spirit, and believes that all people, no matter how damaged, can, with a
                        little willingness, be healed and live happy, productive, fulfilling, and healthy lives.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============================== CTA ============================== -->
    <section class="cta-band" data-aos="fade-in">
        <div class="container">
            <h2>Curious whether we'd be a good fit?</h2>
            <p>You can email, text, or call to set up a free 15-20 minute Zoom consultation. There's no charge, and no
                pressure.</p>
            <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary-filled">Schedule a Free Consultation</a>
        </div>
    </section>